# ShellCheck policy for ThoxOS Ginux Edition (userspace/ginux-edition).
#
# SC2329 (info): "This function is never invoked. Check usage (or
# ignored if invoked indirectly)."
#
# Disposition: disabled in this directory only, because the finding is
# a false positive for the indirect-dispatch pattern used here.
# scripts/local-ci.sh defines full_generation() and passes its name as
# a plain argument to run_step, which executes it through "$@":
#
#     run_step "desktop theme generation in debian:trixie" full_generation
#
# ShellCheck cannot follow that indirection, so it reports the
# function as dead code. The same site already carries an inline
# "shellcheck disable=SC2317" for the same reason: a command reached
# only through run_step looks unreachable to static analysis.
# Deleting or inlining the function to satisfy the checker would be a
# real change chasing a non-bug, so the honest fix is this scoped,
# recorded disposition.
#
# Scope: this file applies to the shell sources checked from this
# directory (make test runs shellcheck on scripts/, docker/,
# installer/, azure/, desktop/ and tests/e2e/ sources). Only SC2329
# is disabled. Every other ShellCheck check stays enabled and must
# pass as part of make test. If a future function in this tree is
# genuinely never invoked, delete it rather than relying on this
# disposition to hide it.
disable=SC2329
